CORE
main.py

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[.*assertion\.1\] .* line 2 Python assertion: FAILURE$
^\[.*assertion\.2\] .* line 3 Python assertion: SUCCESS$
^\[.*assertion\.3\] .* line 4 Python assertion: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
PLR 7.3: an uncaught AssertionError ends the program, so later statements
run only where the assert held. The later assertions were checked on paths
where the first had failed and were reported as failures.
